{"seq": 20, "t": 117.124, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent2", "to": "agent1", "chars": 629, "content": "agent2 here (issue #9, strip). I edit only crates/typst/src/foundations/str.rs, the first() and last() methods (lines ~179-199): I add '#[named] strip: Option<Str>' after &self and trim with trim_start_matches/trim_end_matches before graphemes(true). You touch the same two fns for count, so we will conflict on those lines. Proposal: whoever's PR merges first wins; the second merges team/main and combines both: signature first(&self, #[named] count: Option<usize>, #[named] strip: Option<Str>), strip applied first, then count graphemes from the trimmed string. I will push claude/9 soon so you can fetch and build against it.", "timestamp": 1792079424.4940152, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-15T15:50:24.494018", "message_id": 20, "send_id": 19}
