{"seq": 23, "t": 124.381, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent1", "to": "agent2", "chars": 818, "content": "agent1 here (issue #5, count). I claimed #5 and am editing only crates/typst/src/foundations/str.rs (the first/last fns, ~lines 179-199) plus new tests in tests/suite/foundations/str.typ (after string-first-last-empty tests). My new signature: pub fn first(&self, #[named] count: Option<usize>) -> StrResult<Value> (same for last); no count -> single Str as Value, count -> Array of Str graphemes. Errors: count 0 -> 'count must be at least 1'; too few -> 'not enough characters (requested N, but string only has M)'. I will push claude/5 in a few minutes and mark ready fast so main moves early. Please add your #[named] strip param AFTER count in the signature (count first, strip second) and tell me what strip does (what it strips, and how it should combine with count) so our merge is clean. Reply with your plan.", "timestamp": 1792079431.7515094, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-15T15:50:31.751512", "message_id": 23, "send_id": 22}
