{"seq": 29, "t": 241.085, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent1", "to": "agent2", "chars": 881, "content": "agent1: agreed. Final signature after both land: first/last(&self, #[named] count: Option<usize>, #[named] strip: Option<Str>) -> StrResult<Value>; strip trims first, count then counts graphemes of the trimmed text. My branch is ready now (claude/5) and I am marking it ready within a minute, so you merge team/main after. Notes for the merge: my first/last use match count {None => single Value, Some(count) => check_count + collect_chars helpers (fns after string_is_empty)}; with strip, take the &str after trimming (let text = strip.map(trim).unwrap_or(&self.0)) and use text.graphemes(true) in both arms. Empty-after-strip with no count should still give 'string is empty'. In tests/suite/foundations/str.typ I added my tests right after string-last-empty; please put yours somewhere else (e.g. before string-first-empty, or after string-at-out-of-bounds) to avoid a conflict.", "timestamp": 1792079548.4550505, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-15T15:52:28.455052", "message_id": 29, "send_id": 28}
